I wrote it against the notes: `jumpTo` sets the position and target, then copies `_yaw`/`_pitch` from a scratch `createFreeCamera` aimed at the new view, so the controls continue from it without my guessing the pitch sign convention. Uncertain points:

- I assumed `createFreeCamera`, `attachFreeControl`, and the `scene.camera` setter are all exported from or available on `@babylonjs/lite` as used here; I have not confirmed that.
- I assumed `ObservableVec3` accepts plain `x`/`y`/`z` writes that mark it changed.
- A drag or key move in progress when `jumpTo` runs may coast briefly on the old turn velocity, which I could not reset from the public API.
- `dispose` calls the detach function returned by `attachFreeControl`, which I took to be the only removal for those canvas listeners.
